senses.gloss:
निश्चित a. having settled a thing, resolved upon, sure of
(dat., loc., अर्थम् or —˚);
 settled, fixed upon, certain, n. adv.

निषङ्ग m. quiver or sword (lit. what is attached);
 poss.
˚ङ्गि॑न्.

निषण a. seated;
 sitting, lying, or resting on (loc. or
—˚).

निष॑द् a. sitting inactive;
 n. the state of sitting, esp.
near the altar.

निषध m. N. of a mountain & sev. men;
 pl. N. of a
people.

निषादिन् a. sitting, lying on or in (loc. or —˚);
 m.
elephant-driver.

निषेक m. sprinkling, infusion;
 impregnation ((r.));
 water
used for washing.

निषेव a. practising, frequenting, enjoying;
 devoted to,
intent upon (—˚);
 m., f. निषेवा & निषेव˚न n. as abstr.

निष्क॑ m. (n.) a golden ornament for breast or neck (p.
निष्कि॑न्);
 a. cert. coin.

निष्कम्प a. not trembling, unshaken, immovable;
 abstr.
˚ता f., ˚त्व n.

निष्कर्ष m. drawing out, extracting, taking off (also
˚ण n.);
 extract or essence of anything, main point, chief matter.

निष्कल a. without parts, undivided;
 maimed, impotent,
barren.

निष्कारण a. having no reason, cause, motive, or
purpose;
 ˚—, n., & abl. adv.

निष्क्र॑य m. redemption, ransom, acquittance;
 reward,
wages.

निष्क्रिय a. inactive (abstr. ˚ता f.);
 not performing or
not performed with, ceremonious rites.

निष्ठ a. staying, lying, being, resting, footing,
dependent, or intent upon;
 relating, attached, or devoted to (—˚),
abstr. ˚ता f. — f. आ stand-point, basis, foundation;
 devotion to,
familiarity with (loc.);
 height, summit, close, end (adj. —˚ ending
with);
 decision, sentence, verdict (j.);
 the endings त & तवन्त् and
the participles formed with them (g.).

निष्ठुर a. rough, hard, cruel, merciless;
 abstr. ˚ता
f., ˚त्व n.

निष्पन्न a. come forth, arisen, descended or derived from
(abl.);
 brought about, effected, ripened;
 succeeded, prospered, thriven.

निष्प्रत्याश a. hopeless;
 ˚शी w. भू lose all hope
of (प्रति).

निष्प्रभ a. deprived of light, splendourless, dark,
obscure;
 abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.

निष्प्रयोजन a. having no motive, purpose, or object;
useless, harmless, inoffensive, n. adv.;
 abstr. ˚ता f., ˚त्व n.

निष्फल a. bearing no fruit, fruitless, useless,
unsuccessful;
 abstr. ˚त्व n.

निष्यन्द a. & m. flowing or trickling down;
 m. also
discharge of any fluid, gush, stream.

निस्यन्द a. & m. flowing or trickling down;
 m. also
discharge of any fluid, gush, stream.

निष्षि॑ध् f. preparation, dish, food;
 grant, gift,
oblation.

निसर्ग m. evacuation, discharging (esp. of the body);
giving forth, ceding, granting, bestowing;
 dismission, creation;
 natural
state or character, nature;
 ˚—, instr., & abl. by nature, originally.

निसृष्ट a. hurled on or against (loc. or —˚);
 turned,
directed;
 let loose, dismissed, sent forth;
 kindled (fire);
 committed,
entrusted, granted, bestowed;
 made, accomplished.

निस्तीर्ण a. crossed, passed, overcome;
 saved or escaped
from (—˚).
